            <div xml:id="d1183">

                <pb facs="1187" n="1021" xml:id="pg1021"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.504/85</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Fletcher </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-27T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. See Consul Dawson’s telegram April 26, 5 p.m., relative to increasing strike
                    disorders at Tampico, and refusal of authorities to afford protection.</p>
                <p>Bring matter immediately to attention General Carranza, pointing out to him
                    extreme gravity of situation, and request that orders be telegraphed Tampico
                    authorities to afford adequate protection for American life and property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
